  "case_id": "e20bb7c5-4677-5d6c-a297-05a74bdd8833",
  "finding": "Rows 6934 and 50772 are the same obligation recorded twice: identical supplier, invoice number SFC/24-25/158, amount, item, quantity and officer, with dates only one day apart. The supplier bills many distinct amounts (931 distinct across 939 transactions) with no fixed monthly contract, so a recurring billing pattern cannot explain the repeat. This matches every indicator of a suspected duplicate under SG-PP-4.4 and breaches the unique-invoice rule of SG-PP-4.1.",
  "recommended_action": "Withhold any payment against row 50772 pending review under SG-PP-4.4, confirm with Shah Fabrics & Co that invoice SFC/24-25/158 represents a single obligation, and if a duplicate payment is confirmed recover by set-off under SG-PP-4.5 and record the incident in the duplicate-payment register.",
  "verdict": "likely_true_positive",
  "policy_clauses": [
   "SG-PP-4.4",
   "SG-PP-4.1",
   "SG-PP-4.5"
  ],
